# VG-RASTER (VIRT-GEOM step 12/13): the cluster cut's clusters are HARDWARE-rastered through the material cells (each
# opaque Static group's `.Binned.VirtualGeometry` permutation) into the main pass, and the VG instances are out of the
# main view's bins. Project: F:/BistroFoliageProj. UNVERIFIED (written unbuilt): the VG mesh and the B16 cameras are
# step 21's (below).
# The "bins-only" reference frames: the same steps on commit 92fbdd55d (VG instances drawn by the bins).
# Step 14: per-cut-view candidate regions (each view's cut dispatch covers only its own candidates), the post
# phase's carried clusters packed 64 per workgroup, cascade cuts LOD by the cascade's own texel size.
# Step 13: post phase (a cluster the previous frame's HZB hid is re-cut against this frame's HZB and drawn by the
# GBuffer post pass) and the shadow cascades' own cuts (VG instances out of the cascade bins too).
Проект ../BistroFoliageProj/Desert.deproj --scene Content/Scenes/B16_Bistro_Street.desce
# Step 21: the VG mesh is an EXISTING B16 static mesh made Virtual Geometry by the new asset action "Static Mesh:
# Virtual Geometry on" (UE Asset Actions > Nanite > Enable; ImportOptions::SetStoredVirtualGeometry) over the
# Content Browser selection. Not a lantern: B16's lanterns (BistroExterior_Lantern_Wind_21..25) draw LanternEmissive,
# a StandardSurfaceMasked material, which VirtualGeometryGate refuses (and their entities have CastShadows false).
# The table Paris_Table_01___6__6503 draws only Paris_Table_Terrace (StandardSurface, opaque) and casts shadows;
# its entity (tag Bistro_Research_Exterior_Paris_Table_01___6__6503) stands at world (-66, 37, 570).
# The project must be on MSAS 3 (migrate.sh) for the file to be read. The last step turns the flag off again, so the Bistro repo is left as it was.
Когда run "Content Browser" "Sync to Asset Meshes/Bistro/BistroExterior_Bistro_Research_Exterior_Paris_Table_01___6__6503.stmesh"
Когда run Assets "Static Mesh: Virtual Geometry on"
Тогда [vg_raster] editor.log: "[Import] '...Paris_Table_01___6__6503.stmesh': Virtual Geometry on" and "[VirtualMeshTable] '...Paris_Table_01___6__6503...' registered N clusters" with N > 0, no "Virtual Geometry refused"
Когда run View "View mode: Lit"
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position -316,150,320
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction 0.66,-0.30,0.66
Когда 60 frames render
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Position 184,150,820
Когда --subject viewport set Camera.Direction -0.66,-0.30,-0.66
Когда 1 frames render
Когда shot viewport "vg_raster_cut60.png"
Когда 59 frames render
Когда DesertCtl state views.virtualGeometry
Тогда [vg_raster] views.virtualGeometry.instances >= 1, binnedVgInstances == 0 (main AND cascade views: every cull view has a cut view), clustersDrawn > 0, shadowClustersDrawn > 0 (the sun's cascades draw the table's clusters), overflow 0
Тогда [vg_raster] editor.log: 0 VUID, no "[MeshRenderer] ... has no `.VirtualGeometry` pipeline" for the table's cell, no "the view draws no virtual geometry this frame", no "occluded entries past the post carry's capacity"
Тогда-вид [vg_raster] vg_raster_cut60.png (the frame right after the camera cut, where last frame's HZB is of the other camera): no missing cluster - pixel diff vs the bins-only frame of the same steps < 1% of pixels (pixel diff, not thumbnails)
Тогда-вид [vg_raster] the lit frame at frame 120 shows the table and its shadow as in the bins-only frame: frame mean within 1%
Тогда [vg_raster_views] (step 14: candidates compacted per cut view, post clusters 64 per workgroup, cascade LOD by the cascade's own texel) vg_raster_cut60.png differs from the bins-only frame by < 1% of pixels; views.virtualGeometry.clustersDrawn > 0 and shadowClustersDrawn > 0; editor.log 0 VUID
Тогда [vg_vsm] (step 16: the VSM clipmap levels are cluster cut views, their clusters rastered into the pages; Shadows.Method VirtualMaps, Bistro, 120 frames) views.virtualGeometry.vsmClustersDrawn[level] > 0 on every level that drew pages; the sun shadow (lit frame 120) differs from the bins-only VSM frame by < 1% of pixels (pixel diff); editor.log 0 VUID, no "the virtual shadow map draws its virtual geometry on the CPU walk"
# Step 18-20 [vg_vsm_mixed]: the VSM levels' cluster raster beside their CPU walk. Shadows method = the PPV's request
# (PostProcessVolumeData.Settings.ShadowsMethod: 0 CascadedMaps, 1 VirtualMaps - Common::Scalability::ShadowMethod);
# the quality override `Quality: Shadows.Method` is only a ceiling (default HardwareTraced) and writes machine.json, so
# it is not used. 6039035132485441499 = B16_Bistro_Street's PPV (LOCAL-EXPOSURE-FUSION.scn).
# Step 20 (lead decision, UE: a material with no Nanite path renders the fallback mesh): a VG submesh binned into a VSM
# group whose template declares no `.VirtualGeometry` twin is a FALLBACK (vsmFallbackSubmeshes, walked, no log);
# vsmRefusedGroups counts only a twin the template declares and that has no pipeline. A cooked mesh carries a DAG on
# every submesh or none (VirtualMeshTable.cpp:276-288), so the mix is per section: a section whose VSM caster template
# has no twin. DShaderParser emits the twin for every non-translucent template, and an opaque section casts through
# the default template's shared cell (ShadowCasterCellFor), so a section swapped to any opaque or masked surface stays
# CLUSTERED: the swapped-sections count of fallbacks is 0 for every shipped template (REMAINDER-VIRT-GEOM-20).
Когда set 6039035132485441499 PostProcessVolumeData.Settings.ShadowsMethod 1
Когда 120 frames render
Когда shot viewport "vg_vsm_mixed120.png"
Когда DesertCtl state views.virtualGeometry
Тогда [vg_vsm_mixed] views.virtualGeometry.vsmClustersDrawn: one entry per clipmap level (17), > 0 on every level that drew pages (named per level in the report); views.virtualGeometry.vsmRefusedGroups == 0; views.virtualGeometry.vsmFallbackSubmeshes == the table's sections whose VSM caster template declares no `.VirtualGeometry` twin (0 with the shipped templates); overflow == 0 (the cut of 17 levels fits kMaxVisibleClustersPerCut)
Тогда [vg_vsm_mixed] editor.log: 0 VUID, no "has no `.VirtualGeometry` twin", no "the virtual shadow map draws its virtual geometry on the CPU walk"
Тогда-вид [vg_vsm_mixed] vg_vsm_mixed120.png: the table's shadow - pixel diff of the shadow vs the bins-only VSM frame of the same steps < 1% of pixels (pixel diff, not thumbnails)
Когда set 6039035132485441499 PostProcessVolumeData.Settings.ShadowsMethod 0
Когда 2 frames render
Когда DesertCtl state views.virtualGeometry
Тогда [vg_vsm_mixed] after switching back to cascades: views.virtualGeometry.vsmRefusedGroups == 0 and vsmFallbackSubmeshes == 0 (reset every frame the method is not VirtualMaps)
Когда run View "View mode: Virtual Geometry Clusters"
Тогда-вид [vg_raster] the table shows per-cluster colours on the same silhouette as the lit frame
Когда run View "View mode: Lit"
Когда run "Content Browser" "Sync to Asset Meshes/Bistro/BistroExterior_Bistro_Research_Exterior_Paris_Table_01___6__6503.stmesh"
Когда run Assets "Static Mesh: Virtual Geometry off"
Тогда [vg_raster] editor.log: "[Import] '...Paris_Table_01___6__6503.stmesh': Virtual Geometry off" (the Bistro repo's file back to no clusters)
